{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "240",
   "text": "Is China's centrality to global manufacturing really declining, as the fragmentation narrative suggests?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "241",
   "text": "Bilateral data misleads about global position — rerouting is not displacement",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "242",
   "text": "A correctly measured imbalance ought to drive policy",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "hidden_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "243",
   "text": "\"A large manufacturing surplus requires an offsetting deficit in manufactures elsewhere\" — stated, and used to locate the counterpart",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "accounting_identity",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#ID"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "244",
   "text": "The reported current account \"misleads\" — flagged, with the full case made in the August companion piece",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "source_credibility",
   "toulmin": "backing",
   "oper": "backing",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#SC"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "245",
   "text": "SITC categories 5 through 9, the standard manufactures breakout, from the long UN Comtrade series",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "scope_choice",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#SCP"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "246",
   "text": "Surplus at ~2% of world GDP, above peak Japan and Germany; 80% of solar panels; 35% of manufacturing output against 15% of global output",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#E1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "247",
   "text": "Baldwin on sole manufacturing superpower; Pettis on production giant and consumption pygmy; Bown on the tariff timeline; OECD value-added data",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_source",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#E2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "248",
   "text": "Manufacturing surplus near 2% of world GDP against a reported current account of just 1.5% of China's own GDP",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_discrepancy",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#E4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "249",
   "text": "Policy, not only comparative advantage — resistance to consumer stimulus and a thin safety net sustain a savings surplus",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "250",
   "text": "Upgrading is the stated growth plan, so advanced manufacturing capacity keeps expanding",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "251",
   "text": "The counterpart to the surplus is the United States, not commodity exporters, and the gap keeps widening as a share of world GDP",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "252",
   "text": "Take the IMF's own advice — consolidate 7.5pp of GDP, cut rates, loosen the currency — run it through IMF-derived econometrics, and the current account rises about 4pp of China's GDP. The cure enlarges the disease.",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "policy_reductio",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#C3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "253",
   "text": "The imbalance is large, growing and mismeasured — it shows up everywhere except in the reported current account and in the IMF's analysis",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "254",
   "text": "The size of the imbalance, correctly measured, must be factored into Chinese policymaking and into external policy advice",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "recommendation",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#REC"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "255",
   "text": "The standard view that the post-crisis fall in China's current account means external imbalances are no longer pressing",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "opposing_view",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "256",
   "text": "Specialisation does partly reflect a large population and limited resources; the comprehensive data also lags and misses the 2020-2022 surge",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_mar_10_24#QF"
  },
